# Negative-control variant for the buffer-insensitivity claim of the
# x4buf32 instance: identical in every parameter except
# rosetta_buffer_bytes doubled to 64 MiB. The closed-loop shared-egress
# cells bound worst-case occupancy at 25,432,932 bytes plus packet
# granularity, below both capacities, so the x4buf32 and x4buf64 runs of
# the same cell must be byte-identical (structural row ST-1); any
# difference is an in-flight accounting or loop defect, never hardware
# truth. See merlin_a100_singleswitch_v1_x4buf32.topo for the shared
# provenance and the declared-with-reason buffer statement.
topology dragonfly
hosts_per_router 20
routers_per_group 1
global_links_per_router 0
groups 1
host_link_gbps 200
host_link_latency_ps 300000
switch_pipeline_ps 350000
rosetta_buffer_bytes 67108864
max_wire_packet_bytes 9038
routing_seed 383530136519245852
